	"metadata": {
		"name": "Test Fuel Scenario",
		"description": "Cross-spacecraft fuel transfer: a Tanker servicer (depot tank -> transfer valve -> fuel interconnect) starts docked to a Microsat receiver (fuel interconnect -> fill valve -> main tank). Fuel crosses the docked link while the valve on each side is open. The Microsat also keeps a local fuel-bus harness (RCS tank, valves, feed pump, cold-gas thrusters). GEO over Earth, one ground station."
